                "event": "Rip Current Statement",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Upton NY",
                "headline": "Rip Current Statement issued September 23 at 2:39AM EDT until September 24 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Upton NY",
                "description": "* WHAT...Dangerous rip currents.\n\n* WHERE...Kings (Brooklyn), Southwest Suffolk, Southeast Suffolk\nand Southern Queens Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Life-threatening rip currents are likely for all\npeople entering the surf zone. Anyone visiting the beaches\nshould stay out of the surf. Rip currents can sweep even the\nbest swimmers away from shore into deeper water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The high rip current risk is expected to\npersist through late week.",
                "instruction": "If you enter the surf zone, always have a flotation device with\nyou and swim near a lifeguard. If caught in a rip current, relax\nand float, and do not swim against the current. If able, swim in\na direction following the shoreline. If unable to escape, face\nthe shore and yell or wave for help.",
                "response": "Avoid",
